The platform adaptation says: original interface dt (IEC date time type alias) renamed to scanSeconds; unit seconds, type and original numeric assertion unchanged. So we just use LREAL.

Now produce ST code:

```
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB
VAR_INPUT
    enable : BOOL;
    resetBtn : BOOL;
    scanSeconds : LREAL;
    steamFlow : LREAL;
    fuelFlow : LREAL;
    steamTemp : LREAL;
    steamPressure : LREAL;
END_VAR

VAR_OUTPUT
    qualified : BOOL;
    dataFault : BOOL;
    qualifiedTon : LREAL;
    fuelTon : LREAL;
    revenue : LREAL;
    cost : LREAL;
    netProfit : LREAL;
END_VAR

VAR
    prevResetBtn : BOOL := FALSE;
    // internal accumulators could be retained across scans
END_VAR

// Implementation
// Detect rising edge of reset
VAR_TEMP
    risingReset : BOOL;
END_VAR

risingReset := resetBtn AND NOT prevResetBtn;

// Fault detection
dataFault := (scanSeconds <= 0.0) OR (scanSeconds > 10.0)
             OR (steamFlow < 0.0) OR (steamFlow > 90.0)
             OR (fuelFlow < 0.0) OR (fuelFlow > 6.0);

// Qualified detection
qualified := (steamTemp >= 447.0) AND (steamTemp <= 453.0)
             AND (steamPressure >= 3750.0) AND (steamPressure <= 3850.0);

// Reset logic: rising edge clears accumulators and does NOT accumulate this scan
IF risingReset THEN
    qualifiedTon := 0.0;
    fuelTon := 0.0;
ELSE
    // Only accumulate if enable and no fault
    IF enable AND NOT dataFault THEN
        // Fuel always accumulates
        fuelTon := fuelTon + fuelFlow * scanSeconds / 1000.0;
        // Qualified steam accumulates only if qualified
        IF qualified THEN
            qualifiedTon := qualifiedTon + steamFlow * scanSeconds / 1000.0;
        END_IF;
    END_IF;
END_IF;

// Update revenue, cost, netProfit each scan
revenue := qualifiedTon * 280.0;
cost := fuelTon * 1500.0;
netProfit := revenue - cost;

// Update previous resetBtn for next scan
prevResetBtn := resetBtn;
```

We need to ensure that qualifiedTon and fuelTon are non-negative. If any negative value occurs erroneously due to programming error, they might become negative. But we can enforce:

```
IF qualifiedTon < 0.0 THEN qualifiedTon := 0.0; END_IF;
IF fuelTon < 0.0 THEN fuelTon := 0.0; END_IF;
```

But not necessary. We'll add for safety.

Now we need to ensure that when risingReset is true, we set accumulators to 0, and we must not also add for that scan. Our logic does that.

Now about detection of data fault: When dataFault true and risingReset false, we skip accumulation. Good.

Now about resetting the accumulators only on rising edge; if reset button is held, we don't clear each scan. Since risingReset only true when transitioning from false to true, that matches.

Now about "仅在没有复位上升沿时保持累计值": We maintain previous values.

Now about "公开输入和累计输出的增量及收入成本关系；复位拍不累计，浮点容差 1e-6": Already satisfied.

Now about "平台适配：原接口 dt（IEC 日期时间类型别名）统一重命名为 scanSeconds；单位秒、类型及原数字断言不变": Done.

Now about "qualifiedTon, fuelTon, revenue, cost 必须非负；netProfit 允许为负". So we set revenue and cost as product of non-negative accumulators, which will be non-negative. We'll also enforce that revenue and cost cannot be negative due to rounding errors, but not needed.

Now about "复位上升沿优先于禁用及数据故障。当拍清零且不累计。无复位沿时禁用或故障冻结累计量；判定位和金额仍按当拍更新。" Our logic matches: If risingReset, we clear and skip accumulation; else, if disabled or fault, we skip accumulation. We still compute qualified and dataFault outputs and revenue, cost, netProfit each scan.

Now we must provide final code with function block name FB.

Make sure to include VAR and VAR_END.

